# Cloudflare Pages reads this file and sends these headers with every file it
# serves. It is not part of the game: delete it and the ranch still works, it is
# just served with Cloudflare's own defaults.
#
# WHY no-cache. The game is plain index.html plus /js/*.js, and none of those
# names ever change when the code inside them does. Without this, a phone that
# played yesterday would happily keep playing yesterday's game - and worse, it
# could end up with a new index.html and an old main.js, which is the kind of
# half-and-half that breaks in a way nobody can explain.
#
# "no-cache" does NOT mean "do not keep a copy". It means "keep it, but ask me
# first" - so a phone with nothing new to fetch still starts instantly, and a
# phone with something new to fetch gets it. That is exactly what a small game
# that is still being changed wants.
#
# nosniff tells the browser to believe the file type it was given rather than
# guessing from the contents, which is one less thing that can ever go odd.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
